      "text": "To determine the values of \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in the equation of the line \\(y = ax + b\\), we can use the given points \\((4, 5)\\) and \\((8, 17)\\). Substituting these points into the equation, we get two equations with the variables \\(a\\) and \\(b\\).\n\nFor the point \\((4, 5)\\):\n\\[ 5 = 4a + b \\]\n\nFor the point \\((8, 17)\\):\n\\[ 17 = 8a + b \\]\n\nWe now have a system of linear equations:\n\\[ \\begin{cases} \n4a + b = 5 \\\\\n8a + b = 17 \n\\end{cases} \\]\n\nTo find \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), we can subtract the first equation from the second to eliminate \\(b\\):\n\\[ (8a + b) - (4a + b) = 17 - 5 \\]\n\\[ 8a + b - 4a - b = 12 \\]\n\\[ 4a = 12 \\]\n\\[ a = 3 \\]\n\nNow we can substitute \\(a = 3\\) back into the first equation:\n\\[ 4(3) + b = 5 \\]\n\\[ 12 + b = 5 \\]\n\\[ b = 5 - 12 \\]\n\\[ b = -7 \\]\n\nThus, we have \\(a = 3\\) and \\(b = -7\\). Therefore, \\(a - b = 3 - (-7) = 3 + 7 = 10\\).\n\nThe final answer is \\(\\boxed{10}\\).\n\nLet's confirm this with Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\nfrom sympy import symbols, Eq, solve\n\n# Define the variables\na, b = symbols('a b')\n\n# Define the equations based on the points (4, 5) and (8, 17)\neq1 = Eq(4*a + b, 5)\neq2 = Eq(8*a + b, 17)\n\n# Solve the system of equations\nsolution = solve((eq1, eq2), (a, b))\na_val = solution[a]\nb_val = solution[b]\n\n# Calculate a - b\nresult = a_val - b_val\nprint(result)\n```",
